{
  "comment": "@spec AUTOMATED-REMEDIATION-12 @spec AUTOMATED-REMEDIATION-17 @spec AUTOMATED-REMEDIATION-26. The declared-read predicate (maintainer ruling 2026-10-07: one RFC 6901 JSON pointer and a closed comparator set, not an expression language), frozen across three images: the runner's pointer extraction (the `read` phase answers only the sample, never the result), the worker's sample report to the API, and the API's evaluator. `extractions`: given a read tool's `structured` content (null when the tool returned none), its `content` blocks and `is_error`, the runner applies the pointer to the structured content when present, and otherwise, when `content` is exactly one block of type text whose text is strict JSON (no NaN or Infinity; maintainer ruling M3, 2026-10-07), to that parsed JSON; any other shape is `result_unstructured`. It yields `sample`, one of `sample_kinds`, with `value` the pointed JSON scalar for `value` and null otherwise. A scalar whose compact JSON text (ensure_ascii false) exceeds `value_max_chars` code points is `value_too_long`. `successful` names the kinds a verifier counts as a sample taken (AUTOMATED-REMEDIATION-18); the others are unsuccessful samples, never refusals. `invalid_pointers` are refused at policy write (policy_document_invalid) and by the runner (invalid_request, without dialing). `sample_report` is the worker's body for `POST /action-executions/{id}/samples`: the fence and the sample and value exactly as the runner answered. One read execution is one sample (maintainer ruling M2), so the body carries no index: the execution is the sample. `evaluations`: the API evaluator's `result` (one of `results`) for a declared `comparator` and `value` (no `value` for `absent`) against a reported sample. Ordering comparators apply only when both sides are numeric (a JSON number, or a string matching `numeric_string_grammar`: optional sign, ASCII digits, optional fraction, optional exponent, nothing else; booleans are never numeric), compared by numeric value; otherwise an ordering comparator is unsatisfied. eq, ne and in never coerce: they compare JSON numbers numerically and everything else by type and value exactly. Read by runner/tests/test_runner_execute_vector.py (the extraction cases and invalid pointers, through the real `read` phase), apps/worker/tests/test_remediation_predicate_vector.py and apps/api/tests/test_remediation_predicate_vector.py, each of which rejects an unknown key.",
